  "correct": "3",
  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\nLogic: (2nd number + 3rd number) **÷ 2 - 101** = 1st number.\n\nNow,\n\nFor (812, 879, 947)\n\n→ (879 + 947) ÷ 2 - 101\n\n→ 1826 ÷ 2 - 101 \n\n→ 913 - 101 = 812.\n\nFor (648, 715, 783)\n\n→ (715 + 783) ÷ 2 - 101\n\n→ 1498 ÷ 2 - 101 \n\n→ 749 - 101 = 648.\n\nSimilarly, for **(612, 679, 747)**\n\n**→ (679 + 747) ÷ 2 - 101**\n\n**→ 1426 ÷ 2 - 101 **\n\n**→ 713 - 101 = 612.**\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option 3\".\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/c76c13ba2d2ab46b47f8a931ae621dac081a0cb266b142dc23f58659fac4a466.png] **__Alternate Method__**Logic: **1st number + 67 = 2nd number;**\n\n**2nd number + 68 = 3rd number.**\n\nFor (812, 879, 947)\n\n→ 812 + 67 = 879\n\n→ 879 + 68 = 947.\n\nFor (648, 715, 783)\n\n→ 648 + 67 = 715\n\n→ 715 + 68 = 783.\n\nSimilarly, for (612, 679, 747)\n\n→ 612 + 67 = 679\n\n→ 679 + 68 = 747.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option 3\".",
